open-iscsi on FenrirOS
======================

iscsiadm, iscsid, iscsistart, iscsiuio and iscsi-iname. Nothing runs by
default: the dinit services /etc/dinit.d/iscsid (and iscsid-initiatorname,
which it needs) are not enabled, and no initiator name is shipped.

1. Initiator name: the first start of iscsid writes a unique one to
   /etc/iscsi/initiatorname.iscsi (iscsi-gen-initiatorname; taken from the
   kernel command line, rd.initiatorname=, or iBFT when present). To choose
   your own, write it before the first start:
     echo "InitiatorName=iqn.2026-01.org.example:host1" > /etc/iscsi/initiatorname.iscsi
2. Kernel module: modprobe iscsi_tcp (or list it in /etc/modules-load.d/).
3. Start iscsid, and enable it at boot if wanted:
     dinitctl start iscsid
     dinitctl enable iscsid
   Or let the tools start it when needed: in /etc/iscsi/iscsid.conf set
     iscsid.startup = /usr/sbin/dinitctl start iscsid
4. Discover and log in:
     iscsiadm -m discovery -t sendtargets -p <portal>
     iscsiadm -m node --login
   CHAP credentials, if the target needs them, go in /etc/iscsi/iscsid.conf
   (node.session.auth.*) or per node with iscsiadm -m node -o update.

The node database is /var/lib/iscsi (created by tmpfiles.d).
